; A separately delegated zone whose parent publishes CAA.
;
; RFC 8659 climbs the *name* tree and does not stop at a zone cut, so a policy
; at caa-child.test governs names inside the delegated child. A resolver that
; halted at the delegation boundary would miss it entirely.
$ORIGIN caa-child.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN CAA  0 issue "parent-ca.test"

; Delegated away to the same server, but a distinct zone. Nothing in it
; publishes CAA, so the climb must cross the cut to find the parent's policy.
inner   IN NS   ns1.test.
